<title>FRANCE: Lafarge 96 net attrib profit 1.85 bln.</title>
<headline>Lafarge 96 net attrib profit 1.85 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   1,846  vs	   2,350</p>
<p>    Net, per share (francs)		   20.5  vs	    26.6</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)		     10.0  vs	    10.0</p>
<p>    Investment				   7,009  vs	   5,942</p>
<p>    Turnover				    35,262  vs	  33,218</p>
<p>NOTE - French building materials group Lafarge gave the results in a statement.</p>
<p>Lafarge chairman Bertrand Collomb said in the statement the company's strategy of growth, competition and widening its presence in several markets were favourable elements for the years to come. &quot;And from 1997, I expect a strong increase in our profits,&quot; Collomb said.</p>
<p>Lafarge shares fell 3.14 percent on Tuesday, underperforming the stock market, ahead of the results. Some analysts feared they could come in lower than in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
